        {"h2_html": "What Housecall Pro <em>does well</em>",
         "body_html": '<p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch">Housecall Pro earned its reputation on the operational side of a home-service business, and that strength is real. As described on its site at the time of writing, and worth checking there for current details, it handles scheduling and dispatch with a drag-and-drop calendar, quotes and invoices, card and bank payments, GPS fleet tracking, and a mobile app that technicians run from the truck. For an owner who wants to sit in the driver seat and run the day themselves, it is a capable, well-built platform, and it covers a lot of ground across dozens of home-service trades.</p><p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch;margin-top:1rem">It is worth being clear about what kind of tool it is, because that is the honest basis for any comparison. Housecall Pro is self-serve software: you and your office staff sign in, set it up, and operate it, whether you are a one-person shop or a larger team. It has broadened over the years and now offers its own website, call-answering, and review features too. Those are still tools you switch on and manage yourself, which is exactly right for owners who want that control.</p>'},
        {"h2_html": "Where Top Shelf is <em>different</em>",
         "body_html": '<p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch">Top Shelf is built around the front office. It is a right-sized CRM with an AI receptionist built in, and we set it up for you, including the questions the receptionist asks and your booking rules. You get one plan instead of a stack of logins to keep up with. The <a href="solution-ai-phone.html">AI receptionist</a> answers every call and books the job straight onto your calendar, and the CRM behind it follows up on every lead automatically, so a missed call or a cold quote does not quietly slip past you.</p><p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch;margin-top:1rem">Two things stay true either way. You own your phone number, your leads, and your data, so what you build stays yours. And Top Shelf is honest about what it is not: it has a simple dispatch board, but it is not a full field-operations suite, so if you want to run deep work orders and technician scheduling yourself, that is not what this replaces. What it replaces is the pile of front-office work, answering, booking, following up, and asking for reviews, that an owner rarely has the time to do well alone.</p>'},
